help_body:
local-speak2text - local offline speech-to-text

[How to use]
- Hold Right-Ctrl and speak; on release the text is typed into the current window;
- Ctrl+Space toggles continuous mode (speak and text keeps flowing); press again to finish; Esc cancels;
- Fully offline - audio never leaves this machine.

[How to add a model]
1. Create a folder under the app's models folder (any name, e.g. my-model);
2. Put model files in by type (auto-detected, no config change needed):
   - Qwen3 family: conv_frontend.onnx + encoder/decoder int8 onnx + tokenizer subfolder;
   - SenseVoice: model.int8.onnx + tokens.txt;
   - FireRedASR: encoder.int8.onnx + decoder.int8.onnx + tokens.txt;
   - Paraformer: model.int8.onnx + tokens.txt;
3. Tray right-click > Choose model folder > pick it.
   Get int8 packages from the sherpa-onnx releases page. Or use
   'Copy model-setup instructions (for an AI assistant)' and let an AI do it for you.

[Benchmark]
Tray right-click > Benchmark models: real recognition speed test (RTF) for every
model under asr-modules\, with a usability verdict and a recommendation. Re-run after changing hardware.

[Where are config and logs]
- Config: %LOCALAPPDATA%\local-speak2text\config.json
- Logs: %LOCALAPPDATA%\local-speak2text\log\
- Perf trace: one line per recognition is appended to the log above.

[Other]
- Tray right-click switches UI language (Chinese/English), autostart, auto gain;
- Check for updates: available once update_repo is configured.
